{
  "_name": "probe-2026-09-21-step3 - the 40-question re-run set",
  "_why": "Run with: manage.py nessie --tier full --cases /app/NessieAI/tests/nessie_tests/probes/probe-2026-09-21-step3.json",
  "_source": ".claude/work/2026-09-21-step3-tickets/QUESTION-SET.md (outside git). Read that for the per-question 'Accept when' column and the SHOULD CHANGE / SHOULD HOLD / STILL OPEN marks.",
  "_criteria_note": "Deliberately loose on wording, strict on numbers. Route where the engine is known, and last_reply nonempty everywhere, so a budget-capped or errored turn cannot score green. The real acceptance is still the 'Accept when' column and is read by a human: most of these are judgements about wording ('never an invented pagination story') that no regex should settle. BUT a case whose truth is a NUMBER now asserts that number, because route-plus-nonempty let two confidently wrong answers score green in the 2026-09-21 run: q10 and q11 both answered 0 against a measured 737. Numbers pinned here and where they come from: 737 = T_MUS carrying a Genotype matching ^CC[0-9], counted live on 2026-09-21 (CC042 427, CC024J 75, CC027J 12, CC045J 12, CC051 12, plus a CC0xx tail); 482 and 13-or-20 = the two step3_mixed cases' measured Pilot A truths. Re-measure 737 before trusting a red on it: writing 'collaborative cross' into the mouse metadata, which the operator was doing on 2026-09-22, changes which query finds them but not the population, so the number holds unless the tagging covers a different set.",
  "_cost_note": "~45 turns. One (step3.cc_big_csv_turn_limit) is deliberately a Container-CC request big enough to hit the 180 s cap: that is the point of it, and CC turns are the expensive ones.",
  "_not_included": "mixed.flow_from_rhesus_lymph_node and mixed.ivbcg_nhp_with_sequencing are NOT in nessie_tests/corpus.json -- they are Pilot A mixed-r4 cases. They are written inline here from PilotAPOC/cases/mixed-r4.json with their measured truths.",
